		"text": "Nri was not a kingdom of conquest. Its priest-king, the Eze Nri, and his travelling agents cleansed abominations, crowned titled men and settled disputes across a large part of Igboland, a ritual authority without an army. The bronzes of Igbo-Ukwu, from about the 9th century, are linked to its early history. Its power faded in the 18th century, and the British ended it in 1911.",
